{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1520638-working-on-a-hunter-of-hunters-compact-need-backstories-blaming-each-faction","id":1520638,"title":"Working on a Hunter of Hunters compact, need backstories blaming each faction","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-14T19:19:16-07:00","id":1520638,"title":"Working on a Hunter of Hunters compact, need backstories blaming each faction","content":"I have been playing around with the idea of writing a compact of mortals who, in some way or another, were collateral damage in the vigil and now hunt the hunters. Anyone from a man whose wife and children were caught in the crossfire while having a picnic, to widows of monsters out for revenge, to bitter adult children of hunters who blame the vigil for their trauma and take it out on their parent's comrades, and often their parents. As a bit of fluff production, and inspiration I want to have a few examples of Joker-style &quot;multiple choice backstories/How I got these scars stories&quot; for each compact and conspiracy that could have been behind the trauma that motivates these Hunters of Hunters. The sort of thing that one of them might monologue to a hunter of the compact or conspiracy their supposed backstory blames during a tense scene.<br /> <br /> Fan Compacts and Conspiracies welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T04:45:02-07:00","id":1520659,"title":"","content":"If I were doing this I might be tempted to make it people who were related to Hunters that fell and became slashers. Like &quot;Uncle Johnny served the vigil for 20 years but when his mind broke instead of getting him help you simply killed him like he meant nothing.&quot; <br /> <br /> If you went that route you could give them dread powers, let them be kind of mini slashers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T10:18:23-07:00","id":1520955,"title":"","content":"Do they also go after monsters, and if not, why not? Do they essentially think the monsters will go away if the hunters are killed off? Do they see themselves as judges of hunters, and trust those they &quot;acquit&quot; to handle the monsters? Do they believe monsters should be left alone? Do they not believe in monsters at all, and think of hunters as a murder-cult?<br /> <br /> If they do go after monsters, why hunters as well? Are other hunters just monsters too? Or are they the aforementioned judges? Do they judge monsters case-by-case and think other hunters are kill-em-all extremists?<br /> <br /> Are they a weird kind of slasher that hates their own kind and sees hunters as a spawning ground for more of them?<br /> <br /> Are they controlled by a supernatural force that wants hunters wiped out?<br /> <br /> Whatever you come up with for this, I would say pick one and lean into it hard. Don't try to come up with something where these perspectives coexist in different factions, or you'll end up with a group that amounts to just killing hunters for the sake of having an enemy that kills hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28116-tzies","name":"Tzies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T17:24:59-07:00","id":1520996,"title":"","content":"Sort of a mix of they\u2019re the judges of hunters, and of the monsters aren\u2019t the ones that hurt them, the hunter compacts and conspiracies are. Some of the names I\u2019ve been experimenting with for them are the forgotten army , the bystanders vengeance, stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-19-2023, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T12:10:28-07:00","id":1522525,"title":"","content":"Hunters that use Abyssal power to hunt mages. They act as Abyssal brokers, selling or auctioning helpful items to those they deem to have worthy causes. They always provide certain items cheap to act as a test, like a book with the Nemesis Continuum, the Hildebrand Recording or Le Livre Rouge. The choose them carefully so the greedy or unWise self destruct.<br /> <br /> But while effective, this method causes collateral damage. The hunter's sibling was killed when the gangster came for the Hildebrand tape, or their family was crippled when the Nemesis Continuum rewrote the laws of reality in their area. Now they want revenge on these callous hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}